<title>USA: Sioux Falls feeder cattle steady, light - USDA.</title>
<headline>Sioux Falls feeder cattle steady, light - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>SIOUX FALLS 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Available offerings feeder steers and heifers sold steady, although not well tested, compared to last Thursday, USDA said. Monday's included many smaller lots ranging from thin fleshed to fleshy back-grounded cattle.  Demand fair. 69 percent over 600 lbs.</p>
<p>Steers: Medium and Large 1: 525-550 lbs 89.00-91.50, 600-650 lbs 89.00-90.00, lot thin fleshed 90.50, lot 679 lbs 77.50, lot 774 lbs 75.00, lot 899 lbs 68.75, package 906 lbs 69.00, 1000-1050 lbs 66.50-68.00, fleshy 1100-1150 lbs 65.00-66.80.</p>
<p>Heifers: Medium and Large 1:  500-550 lbs 77.00-82.50, part load 596 lbs 76.50, lot 560 lbs thin 83.00, lot 632 lbs 79.50, 650-700 lbs 74.75-78.00, 700-750 lbs 73.50-75.75, lot 782 lbs 69.80, lot 811 lbs 70.70, part load 936 lbs 68.30, lot fleshy 1022 lbs 65.30, lot 1071 lbs 61.75.</p>
